# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The largest thing in the tree by far (300+ MB: objects, CMake state, the
# fetched dependencies, the test binaries). Regenerated by ./scripts/setup.sh.
# Why it must stay out: build/ records absolute paths, so committing it makes
# every other machine's build conflict and turns small diffs into huge ones.
build/
host/build/
_deps/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
compile_commands.json
*.o
*.a
ctest --test-dir build

# ── Tools downloaded at install time ──────────────────────────────────────
# yt-dlp is ~3 MB and is re-fetched whenever the distribution's copy is more
# than two weeks old. Committing it would mean every update is a binary blob,
# and a pinned old yt-dlp is exactly what breaks sites — see docs/tools.md.
bin/tools/
tools/

# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The PRIVATE half of the extension key. It is not needed to run dwn on another
# machine: extension/manifest.json carries the public key, and the browser
# derives the id from that. The private half is only needed if you ever want to
# *change* the id. Keep it in a password manager, not in git.
docs/dwn-extension-key.pem
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.keystore

# ── Credentials and machine-specific state ────────────────────────────────
# Never commit a native messaging manifest: it embeds the absolute path of the
# host binary and your extension id, which are per-machine by definition.
*.host.json
dev.dwn.host.json
.env
.env.*
*.local

# ── Runtime artefacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Written by scripts/debug-host.sh while capturing a session.
/tmp/dwn-*
*.log
core
core.*

# ── Editor and OS noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Keep these even if a broad rule above would match them ────────────────
# host/dwn.host.json.example is the checked-in reference. The rule above targets
# the *generated* manifests, which live in ~/.config and are outside the repo.
!host/dwn.host.json.example